<title>USA: Nike Vietnam plant seen abusing labor - paper.</title>
<headline>Nike Vietnam plant seen abusing labor - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nike Inc suspended a manager of its plant in Vietnam following a labor rights group report about worker abuse, USA Today said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Vietnam Labor Watch inspected Nike factories there and found violations of minimum wage and overtime laws, as well as physical mistreatment, the paper said. The report would be released today in New York, it said.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
